-- title:
--   Gauss ring of K contracts to that of K₀
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $5 \le q$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $q$-th root of unity. Let $K$ and $K_0$ be intermediate fields of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ with: $K$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) applied to the $q$-expansion function field over $\mathbb{Q}$ of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ for $H$ the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise images of that field, itself generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the ratios $\mathrm{int}(p_f)/\mathrm{int}(p_g)$ of integral $q$-expansions of two modular forms of equal weight with $\mathrm{int}(p_g) \ne 0$; and $K_0$ the analogous base change of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_0(M')$, with $K_0 \le K$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\mathrm{Frac}(A) = L$, with $q$ in its maximal ideal and $\zeta$ in the image of $A$. Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ and $O_0$ one of $K_0$, each characterised by the Gauss condition: $f$ belongs to it exactly when there are $x, y \in A[[T]]$ with $y$ nonzero modulo the maximal ideal and $f \cdot \hat y = \hat x$ as Laurent series over $L$. Then, for the algebra structure on $K$ over $K_0$ given by the inclusion, an element $x \in K_0$ has $\mathrm{algebraMap}(x) \in W_0$ if and only if $x \in O_0$.
--
--   This records the compatibility of the Gauss (Igusa) valuation rings at the cusp $\infty$ on the $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ level with the one on the $\Gamma_0(M')$ floor: $W_0$ lies over $O_0$, so that $O_0$ is the contraction of $W_0$ along $K_0 \le K$. It is used in the analysis of the local behaviour at $\infty$ of the covering of modular function fields, where the residue field of $W_0$ over that of $O_0$ is shown to be separable.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_algebraMap_mem_gauss_iff_of_levelH.lean

